{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>He found him in a desert land.</b> Your father acquired you:" "The sense of <b>יִמְצָאֶהוּ</b> is that in the wilderness the Glory entered with them. Furthermore, they were in the wilderness like a lost man in a wilderness through which no person had passed, for so it is written: וּבְמִדְבַּר תֹּהוּ (and in a desert of waste)." "<b>Howling.</b> A place of howling of animals, such as jackals and ostriches, from whose voice the hearer is frightened." "<b>He encircled him.</b> By the clouds." "<b>He instructed him.</b> The Torah." "<b>He guarded him.</b> From the enemies." "<b>Like the apple of his eye.</b> I have already explained אִישׁוֹן." "The sense of <b>his eye</b> is according to the language of human beings, and the meaning is that He would guard them from every enemy and ambusher."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:25:53.086090451Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}